hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2838","I am among them? Did You not promise me that You would not punish them as long as we seek forgiveness from You?” When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed the prayer, the sun became bright again. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, praised and glorified Allah, and said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. When these two are eclipsed, then turn towards the remembrance of Allah.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Paradise was presented before me, so much so that if I wished, I could have taken a bunch from it. And Hell was presented before me, so much so that I tried to avoid it, fearing that it might engulf you. So I began to say: Did You not promise me that You would not punish them as long as I am among them? O my Lord! Did You not promise me that You would not punish them as long as we seek forgiveness from You?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in it a black woman from Himyar who was the owner of a cat. She had tied up the cat and did not give it anything to eat or drink, nor did she let it go so that it could eat on its own. I saw that whenever she came, her face was scratched. I also saw in Hell a man from the tribe of Da‘d‘a‘ who was the caretaker of the Prophet’s sacrificial animals; he was being thrown into Hell with two sticks having two ends. I also saw a man with a staff; I saw him in Hell, leaning on his staff."
"2839","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on the day the sun was eclipsed, bowing four times in two rak'ahs and prostrating four times. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1469)"
"2840","'Amrah told him that Aishah told her that a Jewish woman came to her and said: ""May Allah protect you from the torment of the grave."" Aishah said: ""O Messenger of Allah, will people be tormented in the graves?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought refuge with Allah. 'Aishah said: ""The Prophet ﷺ went out, and the sun became eclipsed. We went out to another room and the women gathered with us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and that was at the time of forenoon. He stood for a long time, then he bowed for a long time, then he raises his head and stood for a shorter time than the first one; then he bowed for a shorter time than the first one. Then he prostrated, then he stood up for the second (rak'ah) and did the same again, except that his bowing an prostrating were shorter than in the first rak'ah. Then he prostrated, and the eclipse had ended. When he had finished, he sat on the minbar and one of the things he said was: 'The people will be tried in their graves like the trial of the Dajjal.' Aishah siad: 'After that, we used to hear him seeking refuge with Allah (SWT) from the torment of the grave."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1475)"
"2841","I have seen it while standing in this place. And I wished to take a bunch from Paradise—this happened when you saw me move forward. And I also saw Hell, parts of it consuming other parts—this happened when you saw me retreat. I saw in Hell Amr bin Luhayy, the one who started the practice of dedicating animals in the name of idols."
"2842","""There was an eclipse of the sun and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to call out: As-salatu jami'ah (prayer is about to begin in congregation). The people gathered and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer. He said the takbir, then he recited at length. Then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time, as long as he had recited or longer. Then he raised his head and said: Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears those who praise Him) Then he recited at length, but it was shorter than the first time, then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time, but it was shorter than the first time. Then he raised his head and said: 'Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then he said the takbir and prostrated for a long time, as long as he had bowed or longer. Then he said the takbir and raised his head, then he said the takbir and prostrated. Then he said the takbir and stood up, and recited for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he raised his head and said: Sami' Allahu liman hamidah. (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then he recited for a long time that was shorter than the first recitation in the second standing. Then he said the takbir and bowed for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he raised his head and said: Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then he said the takbir and prostrated for a long time that was shorter than the first time. Then he recited the tashahhud, then he said the taslim. Then he stood before them and praised and glorified Allah, then he said: 'The sun and the moon do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone, but they are two of the signs of Allah (SWT). Whichever of them becomes eclipsed, turn to Allah (SWT), the Mighty and Sublime, and pray.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1497)"
"2843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer. He (peace and blessings be upon him) stood for a long time, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed (in ruku‘), then he (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) stood again, but this standing was shorter than the first one, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) went into ruku‘ again, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) stood again, but this standing was shorter than the previous one, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) went into ruku‘, so these became three ruku‘, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) went into prostration, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ruku‘ three times, and the standing between them was shorter than the previous standing, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) went into prostration, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) completed the prayer, and during this time the sun had become bright again. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life; these two are among the signs of Allah. When you see them in the state of eclipse, then perform prayer until the eclipse is over.”"
"2844","There was an eclipse of the sun in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had died. The people began to to say that there was an eclipse on account of the death of Ibrahim. The Prophet ﷺ stood up and led the people in prayer performing six bowings and four prostrations. he said: Allah is most great, and then recited from the Qur'an and prolonged the recitation. He then bowed nearly as long as he stood. He then raised his head and recited from the Qur'an but it was less than the first (recitation). He then bowed nearly as long as he stood. He then raised his head and then recited from the Quran for the third time, but it was less than the second recitation. He then bowed nearly as long as he stood. he then raised his head and then recited from the Qur'an for the third time, but it was less than the second recitation. he then bowed nearly as long as he stood. Then he raised his head and went down for prostration. he made two prostrations. He then stood and made three bowings before prostrating himself, the preceding bowing being more lengthy than the following, but he bowed nearly as long as he stood. He then stepped back during the prayer and the rows (of the people) too stepped back along with him. Then he stepped forward and stood in his place, and the rows too stepped forward. he then finished the prayer and the sun had become bright. He said: O people, the sun and the moon are two of Allah's signs; they are not eclipsed on account of a man's death. So when you see anything of that nature, offer prayer until the sun becomes bright. The narrator then narrated the rest of the tradition. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1178)"
"2845","'The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the people in prayer. He stood for a long time, then he bowed for a long time, then he stood for a long time, but it was shorter than the first standing, then he bowed for a long time but it was shorter than the first bowing. Then he stood up, then he prostrated, then he did the same in the second rak'ah, and when he finished the eclipse had ended. Then he addressed the people; he praised and glorified Allah (SWT), then he said: The sun and the moon are two of the signs of Allah (SWT). They do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone. If you see that then call upon Allah (SWT), the Mighty and Sublime, and magnify Him, and give charity. Then he said: 'O Ummah of Muhammad! There is no one more jealous than Allah (SWT), the Mighty and Sublime, when his male or female slave commits zina. O Ummah of Muhammad! By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1474)"
"2846","""There was an eclipse of the sun during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood and prayed, standing for a very long time, then he bowed for a very long time. Then he stood up and (remained standing) for a very long time, but shorter than the first time. Then he bowed for a very long time, but shorter than the first time. Then he prostrated, then he raised his head and stood for a long time, but it was shorter than the first time. The he stood up and (remained standing) for a long time, but it was shorter than the first time. Then he prostrated, and when he finished his prayer, the eclipse had ended. He addressed the people and praised and glorified Allah, then he said: 'The sun and the moon do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone. If you see that then pray, give in charity, and remember Allah, the Mighty and Sublime.' And he said: 'O Ummah of Muhammad! There is no one who is more jealous than Allah (SWT) when His male or female slave commits Zina. O Ummah of Muhammad, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1500)"
"2847","The Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up in a state of anxiety, then he (peace be upon him) said: ""These are signs which Allah sends. They do not appear because of anyone's death or life, rather Allah sends them to instill fear in His servants. When you see any of these things, turn towards the remembrance of Allah and seek forgiveness from Him."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him) that ""turn towards His remembrance"" means the prayer of eclipse (Salat al-Kusuf), because the word ""remembrance"" (dhikr) is used for prayer, or because there is remembrance of Allah in it. Therefore, the word ""remembrance"" is used for prayer."
"2848","The narrator says: I went to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) at that time, and he was performing prayer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) had raised both his hands, he was reciting « » , and supplicating, until when the eclipse ended, he recited two surahs and then performed two rak‘ahs."
"2849","""The Prophet prayed the eclipse payer, and he recited aloud in it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 563)"
"2850","Aishah said: ""The sun was eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and it was called out: 'As-salatu jam'iah (prayer is about to begin in congregation).' So the people gathered and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer, bowing four times in two rak'ahs and prostrating four times."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1473)"
"2851","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the eclipse prayer, and we did not hear his voice.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1264)"
"2852","When, a boy from the Ansar and I were shooting (arrows) towards two of our targets, the sun was sighted by the people at the height of two or three lances above the horizon. It became black like the black herb called tannumah. One of us said to his companion: Let us go to the mosque; by Allah, this incident of the sun will surely bring something new in the community of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As we reached it, we suddenly saw that he (the Prophet) had already come out (of his house). He stepped forward for a long time as much as he could do so in the prayer. But we did not hear his voice. He then performed a bowing and prolonged it as much as he could do in the prayer. But we did not hear his voice. He then prostrated himself with us and prolonged it which he never did in the prayer before. But we did not hear his voice. He then did similarly in the second rak'ah. The sun became bright when he sat after the second rak'ah. Then he uttered the salutation. He then stood up, praised Allah, and extolled Him, and testified that there was no god but Allah and testified that he was His servant and apostle. Ahmad ibn Yunus then narrated the address of the Prophet ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1184)"
"2853","""There was an eclipse of the sun and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and the people with him. He stood for long time reciting something like Surah Al-Baqarah, then he raised (his head) and stood for a long time, then he raised (his head) and stood for a long time which was shorter than the first time. Then he bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he prostrated. Then he got up and stood for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he raised (his head) and stood for a long time, which was shorter than the first time. Then he bowed for a long time, which was shorter than the first time, then he prostrated, then he finished (his prayer) and the sun had been clear. He said: 'The sun and the moon are two of the signs of Allah (SWT) and they do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone. If you see that then remember Allah (SWT) the Mighty and Sublime.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we saw you stretching out your hand when you were standing, then we saw you moving backward. He said: 'I saw Paradise-or it was shown to me- and I reached out to a take a bunch of its fruits. If I ha taken it you would have eaten from it for as long as this world lasts. And I saw Hell and I have never seen anything like it, and I saw that most of its inhabitants are women.' They said: ""Why, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: 'Because of their ingratitude.' It was said: 'Are they ungrateful to Allah?' He said: 'They are ungrateful to their husbands and they are ungrateful for kind treatment. If you are kind to one of them for a lifetime, then she sees (one) bad thing from you, she will say: I have never seen anything good from you.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1493)"
"2854","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed eight bowings (ruku) in the solar eclipse prayer and four prostrations (sajdah). This narration is not authentic because Habib did not hear this narration from Tawus. Similarly, the narration attributed to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the eclipse prayer in this manner is also not correct, because we do not use the ahadith of narrators like Hanish and those similar to him as evidence. Likewise, we also disregard the narrations dictated by them."
"2855","The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to command us to free slaves on the occasion of an eclipse (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1192)"
"2856","The people replied: We bear witness that you (peace and blessings be upon him) have conveyed the message of your Lord and have shown goodwill to your Ummah, and you (peace and blessings be upon him) have fulfilled what was entrusted to you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Some people think that the eclipse of the sun or the moon, or the falling of stars from their rising place, happens due to the death of some great person from the people of the earth. These people are mistaken; rather, these are signs of Allah, through which Allah admonishes His servants so that they may turn to repentance. By Allah! Whatever situation you have to face in your worldly and religious matters, I have just seen it while standing here in prayer. By Allah! The Hour will not be established until the appearance of great liars among you, one of whom will be the one-eyed Dajjal. His left eye will not be there; it will be like the eye of Abu Tuhayya. He was an old man from the Ansar, and there was a wooden stick between him and the chamber of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). Whenever Dajjal appears, he will claim that he is Allah, and whoever affirms and follows him, none of his previous good deeds will benefit him. Soon, Dajjal will dominate the entire earth except for the sacred precincts and Bayt al-Maqdis; he will not be able to conquer them. He will force the Muslims to go towards Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be under severe siege. The narrator named Aswad states: I think these words are also in the narration, that during this time, Sayyiduna Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) will descend among them, and Allah will defeat Dajjal and his armies, until even the foundation of the wall and the trunk of the tree will call out: O believer! This disbeliever is hiding behind me, come forward and kill him. And this will not happen until you see great events that will disturb you. You will ask each other: Did your Prophet mention this to you? It will be such a trial that even mountains will move from their places. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then after that, there will be a seizure. Then he joined the tips of his fingers together. Then he said this a second time: What the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had said, I have seen it. Then he mentioned the same thing and did not change a single word from its place, neither before nor after."
"2857","""A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the livestock have died and the routes have been cut off; pray to Allah (SWT), the Mighty and Sublime.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed to Allah (SWT) and it rained from that Friday until the next. Then a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'The houses have been destroyed, the routes have been cut off and the livestock have died.' He said: 'O Allah, on the tops of the mountains and hills, in the bottom of the valleys and where the trees grow.' So (the rain) was lifted from Al-Madinah like a garment being removed."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1504)"
"2858","""The Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Khutbah one Friday when the people stood up and shouted: 'O Prophet of Allah! There has been no rain and the animals have died. Pray to Allah (SWT) to send us rain.' He said: 'O Allah, send us rain; O Allah, send us rain.' By Allah (SWT), we could not see even a wisp of a cloud in the sky, then a cloud appeared and grew, and it rained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came down and prayed, and the people departed, and it continued to rain until the following Friday. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to deliver the Khutbah, they called out to him and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, the houses are destroyed and the routes are cut off. Pray to Allah to take it away from us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: 'O Allah, around us and not on us!' Then is dispersed from Al-Madinah and rain fell around Al-Madinah but not a single drop fell on Al-Madinah. I looked, and it was in something like a ring."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1517)"
"2859","""There was no rain for a year, so some of the Muslims went to the Prophet ﷺ one Friday and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, there has been no rain; the land has become bare and our wealth has been destroyed.' He raised his hands, and we did not see any cloud in the sky. He stretched forth his hands until I could see the whiteness of his armpits, praying to Allah (SWT) for rain. When we finished praying Jumu'ah, even a young man whose house nearby was worried about how he would get home. That lasted for a week, then on the following Friday they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, houses have been destroyed and all travel has been ceased.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled at how quickly the sons of Adam become weary, and he said with his hands raised: 'O Allah, around us and not on us,' and it dispersed from Al-Madinah."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1527)"
"2860","The people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of the lack of rain, so he gave an order for a pulpit. It was then set up for him in the place of prayer. He fixed a day for the people on which they should come out. Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the rim of the sun appeared, sat down on the pulpit, and having pronounced the greatness of Allah and expressed His praise, he said: You have complained of drought in your homes, and of the delay in receiving rain at the beginning of its season. Allah has ordered you to supplicate Him has and promised that He will answer your prayer. Then he said: Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe, the Compassionate, the Merciful, the Master of the Day of Judgment. There is no god but Allah Who does what He wishes. O Allah, Thou art Allah, there is no deity but Thou, the Rich, while we are the poor. Send down the rain upon us and make what Thou sendest down a strength and satisfaction for a time. He then raised his hands, and kept raising them till the whiteness under his armpits was visible. He then turned his back to the people and inverted or turned round his cloak while keeping his hands aloft. He then faced the people, descended and prayed two rak'ahs. Allah then produced a cloud, and the storm of thunder and lightning came on. Then the rain fell by Allah's permission, and before he reached his mosque streams were flowing. When he saw the speed with which the people were seeking shelter, he ﷺ laughed till his back teeth were visible. Then he said: I testify that Allah is Omnipotent and that I am Allah's servant and apostle. Abu Dawud said: This is a ghraib (rate) tradition, but its chain is sound. The people of Medina recite ""maliki"" (instead of maaliki) yawm al-din"" (the master of the Day of Judgement). But this tradition (in which the word maalik occurs) is an evidence for them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1173)"
"2861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would also supplicate for rain for those people, and they would be granted rain. After the passing of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), a drought occurred, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went out taking Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) along, so that they could supplicate for rain through his means. He said: ""O Allah! Previously, when we were afflicted with drought in the time of Your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), we would supplicate for rain through the means of Your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and You would grant us rain. Now we supplicate to You through the means of the uncle of Your Prophet, so grant us rain."" The narrator says: They were granted rain."
"2862","“One of the chiefs* sent me to Ibn ‘Abbas to ask him about the prayer for rain. Ibn ‘Abbas said: ‘What kept him from asking me?’ He said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out humbly, walking with a humble and moderate gait, imploring, and he performed two Rak’ah as he used to pray for ‘Eid, but he did not give a sermon like this sermon of yours.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1266)"
"2863","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not raise his hands during any supplication except when praying for rain, when he used to raise his hands so high that the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1513)"
"2864","The Prophet ﷺ went out and prayed for rain, then he prayed two rak'ahs in which he recited loudly. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1522)"
"2865","narrates from his uncle that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) went out to perform the prayer for rain (Salat al-Istisqa). He (peace be upon him) faced the Qiblah and turned his back to the people. He (peace be upon him) took off his cloak and performed two rak'ahs in which he recited aloud."
"2866","""Abbad bin Tamim told me that he heard his paternal uncle, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day to pray for rain. He turned his back toward the people, praying to Allah (SWT), and he turned to face the Qiblah. He turned his rida' around, then he prayed two rak'ahs."" (One of the narrators) Ibn Abi Dhi'b said in the hadith: ""And he recited in them both."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1519)"
"2867","The Messenger of Allah (pbuh)prayed for rain wearing a black robe with ornamented border. The Messenger of Allah (pbuh)wanted to reverse it from bottom to top by holding the bottom. But when it was too heavy he turned it round on his shoulders. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1164)"
"2868","Allah, the Exalted, prescribed prayer for you, through the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ, four rak'ahs while resident, two rak'ahs while travelling and one rak'ah in time of danger. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1247)"
"2869","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in offering the fear prayer. One row stood in front of him and another row stood behind him. He led those who were behind in prayer, bowing once and prostrating twice, then they moved forward until they took the place of their companions, and the others came and took their place, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer, bowing once and prostrating twice, then he said the taslim, so the Prophet ﷺ had prayed two rak'ahs and they had prayed one. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1545)"
"2870","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the prayer; one row stood behind him and one row stood facing the enemy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led these people in one rak'ah, then they went and stood in the place of their brothers, and the other group came. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in one rak'ah as well, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the salam. Thus, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed two rak'ahs, and each group performed one rak'ah."
"2871","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed at Dhi Qarad and the people formed two rows behind him, one row behind him and one row facing the enemy. He led those who were behind him in praying one rak'ah, then they went and took the place of the others, and the others came and he led them in praying one rak'ah, and they did not make it up. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1533)"
"2872","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was camping between Dajnan and 'Usfan, besieging the idolaters. The idolaters said: 'These people have a prayer that is dearer to them than their sons and daughters. Plan it, then strike them with a single heavy blow.' Jibril, peace be upon him, came and told the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to divide his companions into two groups, then lead one group in prayer while the others faced the enemy, on guard and with weapons at the ready. So he led them in praying one rak'ah, then they moved back and the others moved forward, and he led them in praying on rak'ah, so that each one of them had prayed one rak'ah with the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ had prayed two rak'ahs."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1544)"
"2873","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the prayer of fear at the place of Dhat al-Riqa. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) divided the people into two groups. One group stood behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and the other group stood facing the enemy. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said the takbeer, the group that had formed rows behind him also said the takbeer. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into ruku, so those people also went into ruku. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into sajdah, so those people also went into sajdah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, so those people also got up. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained seated in his place, and those people themselves performed the second sajdah, and then they stood up and, walking on their heels, moved back until they stood at the rear, and the second group came forward. They formed rows behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Those people said the takbeer, then they themselves performed one rak’ah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the second sajdah, so they performed sajdah along with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up from that rak’ah, and those people themselves performed the second sajdah. Then both groups stood up and formed rows behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into ruku, so they all went into ruku. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into sajdah, so they all went into sajdah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, so those people also raised their heads. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed each of these actions very quickly. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not show any negligence in this regard, and performed ruku and sajdah as briefly as possible. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said salam, so those people also said salam. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, and all the people had participated in the prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"2874","It was narrated from Jabir bin ‘Abdullah that the Prophet ﷺ led his Companions in the fear prayer. He led them all in bowing, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the row nearest him prostrated, and the others stood up, then when he stood up, they prostrated twice by themselves. Then the front row moved back and took their place, and they moved forward until they formed the front row. Then the Prophet ﷺ led them all in bowing, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the row nearest to him prostrated, and when they raised their heads, the others prostrated twice. So all of them bowed with the Prophet ﷺ and some of them prostrated by themselves, and the enemy was in the direction of the Qiblah. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1260)"
"2875","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was present at the place of Usfan, while the polytheists were at the place of Dajnan. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Zuhr prayer, the polytheists saw him bowing and prostrating, so they consulted among themselves that they would attack him. When the time for the Asr prayer came, the people formed two rows behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said the takbir, and all the people also said the takbir. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed, and all the people bowed. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went into prostration, so the row that was standing close to him went into prostration, while the other row, holding their weapons, stood facing the enemy. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, the second row also performed prostration. When they raised their heads, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed, and all the people bowed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prostrated, so the row that was standing close to him prostrated, while the other row, holding their weapons, stood facing the enemy. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, the second row also performed prostration. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) There is a difference of opinion regarding the name of the narrator Abu Ayyash Zurqi. Some have said that his name is Zayd bin Nu’man, and some have said that it is Zayd bin Samit. Some have said it is Ubayd bin Mu’awiyah bin Samit, while others have said it is Ubayd bin Mu’adh bin Samit."
"2876","The commander of the polytheists was Khalid bin Walid. The narrator says: We performed the Zuhr prayer. The polytheists said: These people were in such a state that if we wanted, we could have attacked them (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words:) We could have attacked them in their heedlessness. The narrator says: Between Zuhr and Asr, the verse regarding the command of Qasr prayer was revealed. The people took up their weapons and formed rows behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). They made two rows, their faces towards the enemy and the polytheists facing them. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said the Takbir, and all the people said the Takbir. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed in Ruku, and all the people bowed in Ruku. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, and all of them raised their heads. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Sajdah, so the row that was closest to him performed Sajdah, and the other people kept guarding them. When these people finished their Sajdah, then the other people performed Sajdah. Then the row that was closest to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) moved back, and the other people came forward and stood in their place. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed in Ruku, and all the people bowed in Ruku. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head, and all of them raised their heads. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Sajdah, so the row that was closest to him performed Sajdah, and the other people stood guarding them. When these people finished their Sajdah, then the other people performed Sajdah. Then these people stood straight with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and all of them sat down. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said Salam along with all of them. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led this prayer at the place of Usfan. He (peace and blessings be upon him) led this prayer on the day of confrontation with Banu Sulaym."
"2877","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned this matter to us. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those people are saying, between us and them is this prayer, which is more beloved to them than anything else. When the time for prayer came, we formed two rows. The polytheists were between us and the Qiblah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the takbeer, and we also said the takbeer following him. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into ruku‘, and we also went into ruku‘ with him. When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed sajdah, the first row performed sajdah with him. When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, the second row performed sajdah. Then they moved forward and stood in the place of the first row, and the people of the first row moved back. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the takbeer, and we also said the takbeer with him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into ruku‘, and we also went into ruku‘ with him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed sajdah, the people of the first row performed sajdah with him, then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat down, then the people of the second row performed sajdah, then all of them sat down, and then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ended the prayer with salam along with all of them. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Zubair has transmitted these words. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Just as your leaders perform the prayer."
"2878","Did you pray in time of danger with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? AbuHurayrah replied: Yes. Marwan then asked: When? AbuHurayrah said: On the occasion of the Battle of Najd. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to offer the afternoon prayer. One section stood with him (to pray) and the other was standing before the enemy, and their backs were towards the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ uttered the takbir and all of them too uttered the takbir, i.e. those who were with him and those who were facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered one rak'ah and the section that was with him also prayed one rak'ah. He then prostrated himself and those who were with him also prostrated, while the other section was standing before the enemy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then stood up and the section with him also stood up. They went and faced the enemy and the section that was previously facing the enemy stepped forward. They bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing in the same position. Then they stood up and the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon) prayed another rak'ah and all of them bowed and prostrated along with him. After that the section that was standing before the enemy came forward and they bowed and prostrated, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained seated and also those who were with him. The salutation then followed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ uttered the salutation and all of them uttered it together. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs and each of the two sections prayed one rak'ah with him (and the other by themselves). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1240)"
"2879","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the prayer of fear. He led one group in one rak’ah while the other group remained facing the enemy. Then those people returned and stood facing the enemy. When the others came, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in one rak’ah as well. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said salam with all of them. Then these people went and stood facing the enemy in place of their companions. Then the others came, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in one rak’ah as well. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said salam with all of them, so both these people and those people performed one rak’ah each."
"2880","'Abdullah bin 'Abbas said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and the people stood with him, and he said the takbir and they said the takbir. Then he bowed, and some of them bowed, then he prostrated and they prostrated, then he stood for the second rak'ah and those who had prostrated with him moved back and guarded their brothers, and the other group came and bowed and prostrated with the Prophet ﷺ. All the people were praying and saying the takbir, but they were guarding one another."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1534)"
"2881","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) formed two rows of people. The row that was present with the Prophet (peace be upon him), he led them in two rak‘ahs of prayer, then they said salam and moved back, and the other people came forward. The Prophet (peace be upon him) also led them in two rak‘ahs, then they too said salam. In this way, the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed four rak‘ahs, and these Muslims performed two rak‘ahs each."
"2882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Yes. He asked: Do you not fear me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: No. He asked: Who will protect you from me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Allah Almighty will protect me from you. The narrator says: That man drew his sword, and the people scolded and rebuked him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered the people to depart from there and to take up arms. Then the call to prayer was given. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led the group behind him in prayer, and another group faced the enemy and guarded. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led the group with him in two rak‘ahs, then the other group came and stood in the place where those who had prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had stood, and they turned to face the enemy and began to guard. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also led these people in two rak‘ahs, so in this way the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) completed four rak‘ahs, and his companions performed two rak‘ahs."
"2883","I promise you that I will not fight against you, nor will I be with any people who fight against you. The narrator says: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) let him go. He went back to his companions and said: I have come to you from the best of all people. When the time for Zuhr, or perhaps Asr, came—this doubt is from the narrator Abu Awanah—the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ordered the prayer of fear (Salat al-Khawf). The narrator states: The people formed two groups; one group faced the enemy, and the other group began to pray with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) led the group with him in two rak‘ahs, then they finished their prayer and moved to the place of the other group, and those people came and began to pray behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). They performed two rak‘ahs, thus the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) completed four rak‘ahs, and each of those groups performed two rak‘ahs."
"2884","narrates: We came along with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we reached the place of Dhat al-Riqa’, then it was announced that congregational prayer was about to be held. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led one group in two rak‘ahs, then they moved back and he led the other group in two rak‘ahs, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four rak‘ahs and those people performed two rak‘ahs."
"2885","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Abi Hathmah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the prayer of fear: One group will stand in front of the Imam and the other group will stand behind the Imam. The Imam will lead this group (the one behind him) in one rak'ah and two prostrations. Then this group will remain seated in their place until those people (the other group) perform one bowing and two prostrations (of the second rak'ah). Then those people will go to the place of their companions and their companions wil"
"2887","The Imam will stand, and a group will stand with him. They will perform one rak'ah, and the other group will remain between them and the enemy. Then those who performed one rak'ah with the Imam will go back, and those who have not yet prayed will take their place. Then these people will come and perform one rak'ah with the Imam. Then the Imam will complete his prayer. Each of the two groups will perform one rak'ah separately. If the fear is more severe than this, then the prayer should be performed while walking or riding."",""In the prayer of fear"",""the Imam stands and a group of people stand with him. They all prostrate in one prostration. Another group stays between them and the enemy. Then those who have prostrated with the Imam leave and take the place of those who have not prayed. Those newcomers pray with their Imam in one prostration. Then their Imam leaves and each person from the two groups prays with their own prayer"","" one prostration. If the fear is more severe than that"","" then men or riders should do the same."""""""
"2888","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, one group stood behind him, and another group stood behind them. Those who were standing directly behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were standing, while the other group was sitting. All their faces were towards the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said the takbir, and both groups said the takbir. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ruku‘, and the group behind him also performed ruku‘, while the others remained seated. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed sajdah, so those people performed sajdah, and the others remained seated. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, those people also stood up, and they moved back to the place where their companions were sitting. Then the second group came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in one ruku‘ and two sajdahs, and the others remained seated. Then when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said salam, both groups stood up and each performed one rak‘ah individually. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) There is no contradiction or difference in these narrations; rather, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Salat al-Khawf in different ways on different occasions, as we have mentioned. The intention of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was to teach his ummah the methods of Salat al-Khawf, because it is permissible for them to perform the prayer according to any of these nine methods, just as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the prayer in times of fear. That is, whichever method is suitable according to the situation, it is permissible for a person to perform the prayer in times of fear according to any of these methods that we have mentioned. These belong to the category of permissible differences; there is no contradiction or difference in these narrations."
"2889","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah! We too have not yet performed this prayer. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at the place of Bathan and I was with him. He performed ablution, and after the sun had set and after the time when those who fast have broken their fast, he performed the Asr prayer."
"2890","Sayyiduna Abu Sa’id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him). On the occasion of the Battle of Khandaq, we were engaged (in fighting) until the time after Maghrib had passed. This was before the command regarding fighting was revealed. When our sufficiency regarding the battle was achieved (this refers to the statement of Allah, the Exalted): ""In battle, Allah was sufficient for the believers. Allah is Powerful and Dominant."" (After Maghrib had passed) the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and he gave the Iqamah for Zuhr, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed this prayer just as he would perform it at its (prescribed) time. Then he gave the Iqamah for Asr, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed this prayer just as he would perform it at its (prescribed) time. Then he gave the Iqamah for Maghrib, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed this prayer just as he would perform it at its (prescribed) time."
"2891","They distracted us on the day of al-Ahzab from ʿAsr prayer, until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ʿThey distracted us from the middle prayer, ‘Asr prayer. May Allah fill their graves and houses or stomachs with fire.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1036)"
"2892","Sayyiduna Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib began to discuss the world, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The world is lush and sweet; whoever acquires it along with its due right, there will be blessing in it for him. And there are many people who seek the wealth of Allah and His Messenger, but for them, on the Day of Resurrection, there will be Hell."""
"2893","I served the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for ten years. He never said ""Uff"" to me, nor did he ever say: ""Why did you do this?"" or ""Why did you not do this?"
"2894","I served the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for ten years. He never said ""Uff"" to me, nor ever said: ""Why did you not do this?"" or ""Why did you do this?"
"2895","I did not recognize you."
"2896","the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said, ""˹How˺ wondrous is the affair of a believer: for there is good in every affair of his, while that is not the case with anyone else except in the case of a believer: ˹i.e.,˺ if times of ease strike him, he is grateful which is good for him; and if times of distress strike him, he is patient, which is ˹also˺ good for him."" (Using translation from Muslim 2999)"
"2897","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat up straight in a state of anger. His face turned red. He said: ""Those before you were asked to utter the word (of faith), and if they did not comply, a saw was placed upon them and they were cut into two pieces, but this did not turn them away from their religion. Sometimes, an iron comb was passed through the flesh and nerves of a person until it reached his bones, but even this did not turn them away from their religion. However, you people are showing impatience. Allah will surely complete this matter until a rider will travel from Sana'a to Hadramaut and will fear none except Allah, or the wolf regarding his sheep."
"2898","I do not know what you are saying, but this much is true: Allah Almighty knows that I passed by two men who were arguing with each other and both were mentioning Allah Almighty. I returned home and offered expiation on behalf of both of them, disliking that Allah Almighty's name be mentioned unjustly."" The narrator says, then he went to relieve himself, and when he had finished his need, his wife held his hand. Then one day, she did not come to him, so Allah Almighty revealed to Sayyiduna Ayyub (peace be upon him) at that place: ""Strike your foot; here is cool water to wash and drink."" The woman came to him after some delay, and when Sayyiduna Ayyub (peace be upon him) turned to her, his illness had ended and he was as beautiful (and healthy) as before. When the woman saw him, she said, ""O (sir)! May Allah Almighty bless you, have you seen the Prophet of Allah (Sayyiduna Ayyub, peace be upon him) who was afflicted with illness? By Allah, I have not seen anyone more resembling him than you, that is, when he was healthy."" Sayyiduna Ayyub (peace be upon him) said, ""I am he."" Sayyiduna Ayyub (peace be upon him) had two storehouses, one for wheat and the other for barley. Allah Almighty sent two clouds; one came over the wheat storehouse and rained gold upon it until it was filled (with gold), and the other cloud rained silver upon the barley storehouse until it was filled (with silver), meaning Sayyiduna Ayyub (peace be upon him) became wealthy again."
"2899","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Now, only trials and tribulations remain in the world."
"2900","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The Prophets, then those closest to them (in righteousness), then those closest to them. A person is tested according to the strength of his religion, and the trial continues to be with the servant until it leaves him walking on the earth without any sin upon him."
"2901","“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tested?’ He said: ‘The Prophets, then the next best and the next best. A person is tested according to his religious commitment. If he is steadfast in his religious commitment, he will be tested more severely, and if he is frail in his religious commitment, his test will be according to his commitment. Trials will continue to afflict a person until they leave him walking on the earth with no sin on him.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4023)"
"2902","A child was born into me this night and I named him after the name of my father Ibrihim. He then sent him to Umm Saif, the wife of a blacksmith who was called Abu Saif. He (the Holy Prophet) went to him and I followed him until we reached Abu Saif and he was blowing fire with the help of blacksmith's bellows and the house was filled with smoke. I hastened my step and went ahead of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Abu Saif, stop it, as there comes Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him). He stopped and Allah's Apostle ﷺ called for the child. He embraced him and said what Allah had desired. Anas said: I saw that the boy breathed his last in the presence of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The eyes of Messenger of Allah ﷺ shed tears and he said: Ibrahim, our eyes shed tears and our hearts are filled with grief, but we do not say anything except that by which Allah is pleased. O Ibrahim, we are grieved for you. (Using translation from Muslim 2315)"
"2903","I inform my father of this?"" The woman replied: ""Yes."" So Pharaoh's daughter informed Pharaoh, and Pharaoh summoned the woman and asked her: ""Do you have a Lord other than me?"" The woman replied: ""Yes, my and your Lord is Allah, the Exalted."" So Pharaoh ordered for lead to be melted, and it was melted. The woman said to him: ""I have one request from you."" He replied: ""Alright."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then he began to throw her children one by one (into the fire) until it was the turn of her nursing infant. Then the child said: ""O my mother! Remain steadfast, for you are upon the truth."
"2904","I was taken on the Mi'raj, I passed by a pleasant fragrance. I asked: O Jibreel! What is this? He replied: This is the fragrance of the woman who used to comb the hair of Pharaoh's daughter. Once, while she was combing, the comb fell from her hand, so she said: In the name of Allah (I pick it up seeking blessing). Pharaoh's daughter asked: Do you mean my father? She replied: No, but the Lord of me, you, and your father. Pharaoh's daughter said: I will tell him (i.e., my father). The woman said: Go ahead and tell him. The girl informed Pharaoh, so Pharaoh asked the woman: Do you have any Lord besides me? The woman replied: My Lord and your Lord is He who is in the heavens. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then molten lead was heated for the woman. The woman said to Pharaoh: I have one request from you. Pharaoh asked: What is your request? The woman said: My wish is that you gather my bones and the bones of my children together. Pharaoh said: That will be done, for you have some right over us. Then Pharaoh began to throw her children one by one into the molten lead. At the end, a small child came, and that child said: O my mother, you are upon the truth. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Four children spoke in their infancy: the son of the woman who used to comb Pharaoh's daughter's hair, the child involved in the story of Jurayj, Sayyiduna Isa ibn Maryam, and (the narrator says) I do not remember the fourth child."
"2905","narrate this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whatever trouble, worry, sorrow, pain, grief, or harm befalls a believing servant—even if a thorn pricks him—Allah Almighty, because of that, wipes out some of his sins."
"2906","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whenever a Muslim is pricked by a thorn or suffers anything greater than that (any kind of pain), Allah the Exalted raises his rank because of it and forgives his sins because of it."
"2907","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for a person, He puts him to trial."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: The narrator named Ibn Abu Sa’sa’ah is Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdur Rahman bin Sa’sa’ah, who is among the chiefs of the people of Madinah.)"
"2908","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person has a special rank with Allah Almighty which he cannot attain through any deed, so Allah keeps putting him in a continuous disliked situation until He elevates him to that rank."
"2909","I will supplicate to Allah Almighty for you and He will grant you cure, and if you wish, then be patient, and you will not be taken to account. She said: I will be patient, so that I am not taken to account."
"2910","I was told that Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how could we be in a good state after this verse: “It will not be in accordance with your desires (Muslims), nor those of the people of the Scripture (Jews and Christians), whosoever works evil, will have the recompense thereofʿ fan-Nisa' 4:123]? Will we be punished for every bad deed we do? There Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿMay Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr, do you not fall sick? Do you not get exhausted? Do you not feel sad? Don't calamities befall you?ʿ He said: Of course. He said: ʿThat is the recompense you are given.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 68)"
"2911","The woman said: Stop, for Allah Almighty has abolished polytheism and Islam has come. The man left the woman and turned away. He kept looking back at her, and the woman also kept looking at him, until the man's face struck a wall. He came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with blood flowing from his face and informed him of the entire incident. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are a servant about whom Allah Almighty intended good. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, when Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment for his sin (i.e., in this world), and when He intends evil for a servant, He lets him commit sin until He gives him his full recompense on the Day of Resurrection, as if he is free from sin (i.e., apparently pure)."
"2912","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this affliction is a punishment with which the people before you were punished. When it occurs in a land where you are not present, do not go there, and when it occurs in a land where you are present, do not flee from it."" So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) returned with the people that year. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet Muhammad's (peace and blessings be upon him) informing about the Prophets and previous nations is of three types. The first type is: He praised certain specific things, and the purpose is that this Ummah should act upon those things. The second type is: He mentioned the condemnation of certain things, and his intention is that this Ummah should avoid committing such acts. And the third type is: He described a characteristic, and his intention is that this Ummah should take a lesson from that characteristic."
"2913","""Trials will not cease afflicting the believing man and the believing woman in their self, children, and wealth, until they meet Allah without having any sin."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2399)"
"2914","I not see the Messenger of Allah weeping? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: My weeping is mercy. Every state of the believer is good; when his soul departs from both his sides, at that time he is praising Allah."
"2915","The Similitude of a believer is that of (a standing) crop which the air continues to toss from one side to another; in the same way a believer always (receives the strokes) of misfortune. The similitude of a hypocrite is that of a cypress tree which does not move until it is uprooted. (Using translation from Muslim 2809a)"
"2916","I have never experienced such a condition."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""Do you suffer from headache (suda’)? He asked: ""What is suda’?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""It is a vein that strikes a person in his head."" He said: ""I have never faced such a situation."" When that person left, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever wants to see a person from among the people of Hell, let him look at this man."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Whoever wants to look at a person belonging to the people of Hell, let him look at this man,"" literally informs about a thing, but what is meant is: to prohibit inclining towards that thing and to prohibit lack of patience upon its opposite. The reason is: Allah the Exalted has placed grief and worries in this world so that they may become an expiation for the sins of Muslims. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) wanted to inform his Ummah that a person, during day and night, sometimes does not avoid those things from which Allah the Exalted has prohibited, and because of this, Hell becomes obligatory for him, and he does not seek forgiveness afterwards. Thus, every person is held in pledge for his deeds, and these ailments become an expiation for some of his sins in this world. This does not mean that whoever is granted well-being in this world is from the people of Hell."
"2917","I said, ""By Allah! I will surely inform Allah's Messenger about this."" I informed the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: ""May Allah have mercy on Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him); he was harmed with more than this, but still he remained patient."
"2918","""I have not seen ailment effecting anyone worse than upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2397)"
"2919","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was afflicted with pain, he would become restless and turn about on his bed. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said in his service: If any of us had done this, you (peace be upon him) would have expressed displeasure at it. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Hardship befalls the righteous; whenever a believer is pricked by a thorn, or suffers any pain besides that, due to it his sins are wiped away and his rank is elevated. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Isa bin Abu Kathir made a mistake in narrating the name of the narrator as Abdullah bin Naseeb. The real name is Abdullah bin Harith, and he is the nephew of Ibn Sirin, but he could not transmit the word Harith and instead mentioned Abdullah bin Naseeb."
"2920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The Prophets, then those closest to them (the righteous), and people are tested according to the strength of their religion. The one whose religion is strong, his trial is severe; the one whose religion is weak, his trial is also weak. A person remains in trial until he walks among the people and there is no sin upon him (i.e., due to the trial, his sins are forgiven)."
"2921","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The Prophets, then those closest to them (in righteousness), then those closest to them. A person is tested according to the strength of his religion, and the trial continues to be with the servant until he walks upon the earth having no sin left upon him."
"2922","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Trials come to the one who loves me faster than floodwaters rush towards their destination."
"2923","The man said: Will we be recompensed for everything we do? In that case, we will be doomed. This was reported to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so he said: Yes! A person will be recompensed for it in the form of trials in this world—those trials which afflict his body and cause him pain."
"2924","""Trials will not cease afflicting the believing man and the believing woman in their self, children, and wealth, until they meet Allah without having any sin."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2399)"
"2925","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whatever illness or hardship befalls a believer, it becomes an expiation for his sins, even if it is a thorn that pricks him or any sharp thing that harms him (these too become expiation)."
"2926","The command of Allah, the Exalted, is:) ""Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr! May Allah have mercy on you, do you not fall ill? Do you not suffer pain? Do you not face troubles? These are the things for which you will be recompensed. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The father of the narrator Abu Bakr bin Abu Zuhair is a Companion."
"2927","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever a believing man or woman falls ill, or (the narrator is in doubt or perhaps these are the words) a Muslim man or woman falls ill, Allah Almighty, because of that, wipes away their sins just as a tree sheds its leaves."
"2928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They become an expiation (for sins)."" He asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), even if they are minor?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even if it is a prick of a thorn or less than that."" The narrator says: That person prayed for himself that he would have fever until his death, but that the fever would not prevent him from Hajj, Umrah, striving in the way of Allah, or congregational prayer. The narrator states: Whoever touched his body would feel its heat, until that person passed away. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The female narrator named Zainab is Zainab bint Ka'b bin Malik, and the person who prayed for himself was Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2929","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person travels or falls ill, Allah Almighty records for him the same reward as he used to receive for the deeds he performed while residing at home and in good health."
"2930","I take away two beloved things (i.e., eyesight) from My servant and he remains patient and hopes for reward, then I am not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise."
"2931","I take away from My servant his two beloved things (i.e., the eyesight of both eyes) and he still desires them, then when he praises Me over this, I am not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise."
"2932","narrates this statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whenever Allah Almighty takes away two beloved things (that is, eyesight) from a servant, and that servant acts with patience and hopes for reward, then Allah Almighty will admit him into Paradise."
"2933","The other person said: You have spoken the truth. Then the narrator named Hawzi said: Yes."
"2934","“A man died in Al- Madinah, and he was one of those who were born in Al-Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ offered the funeral prayer for him and said: “Would that he had died somewhere other than his birthplace.” A man among the people said: “Why, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “If a man dies somewhere other than his birthplace, a space will be measured for him in Paradise (as big as the distance) from the place where he was born to the place where he died.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1614)"
"2935","I am Umm Miladim (Mother of Heat). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Go towards Quba and stay there. The narrator says: It went there and the people began to suffer from fever (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) and they faced great hardship because of it. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Have you noticed how much fever we are suffering from? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you wish, I will pray to Allah Almighty and He will remove it from you, and if you wish, it will become a means of purification for you. So they said: Let it remain as a means of purification for us."
"2936","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever a believer falls ill, (that illness) purifies him just as a furnace purifies the rust from iron."
"2937","I visited Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he was running a high temperature. I touched his body with my hand and said to him: Messenger of Allah, you are running a high temperature, whereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Yes, it is so. I comparatively have a more severe fever than any one of you. I said: Is it because there is a double reward in store for you? Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Yes, it is so. And Messenger of Allah ﷺ again said: When a Muslim falls ill, his compensation is that his minor sins are obliterated just as leaves fall (in autumn). In the hadith transmitted on the authority of Zubair there is (no mention of these words):"" I touched his body with my hands."" (Using translation from Muslim 2571a)"
"2938","Umm Sa'ib or Umm Musayyib. why is it that you are shivering? She said:"" It is fever and may it not be blessed by Allah, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: Don't curse fever for it expiates the sin of the children of Adam just as furnace removes the alloy of iron. (Using translation from Muslim 2575)"
"2939","""A woman came to me with two daughters. She was asking (for food) but I did not have anything with me except a date. So I gave it to her and she divided it between her two daughters without eating any of it herself. Then she got up to leave, and the Prophet entered, and I informed him about her. So the Prophet said: "" Whoever is tested something from these daughters (and he/she passes the test), they will be a screen for them from the Fire."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1915)"
"2940","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) at the place of Rabadhah. I asked: O Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), what is your wealth? He replied: My wealth is my deeds. I said: Please narrate to us a hadith which you have heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “If any Muslim’s three children die before reaching maturity, Allah, due to His mercy and grace upon those children’s parents, will admit them both (i.e., the parents) into Paradise.”"
"2941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You will meet me at the house of such-and-such woman."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came there and kept talking with the women. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If any of you has three children who die and she hopes for reward (from Allah), she will enter Paradise."" One of the women asked, ""What about the one who has two?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The one who has two (children who die)?"" (She will also receive this reward and recompense.)"
"2942","""No Muslim, three of whose children die, will be touched by the Fire, except in fulfillment of the (Divine) oath."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1875)"
"2943","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever from among his children loses three (and hopes for reward), he will enter Paradise."
"2944","The women said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! The men have gone ahead of us, so please appoint a day for us as well."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised them a day. The women gathered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave them advice and admonition. Among the things the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them was this: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Any woman whose three children die, they will become a barrier for her from Hellfire."" A woman asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! What if there are two?"" (The narrator says) That woman had lost two children. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her, ""Even if there are two (the same reward and virtue will be attained)."
"2945","""There is no man whose two daughters reach the age of puberty and he treats them kindly for the time they are together, but they will gain him admittance to Paradise."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3670)"
"2946","The narrator says: We asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! What if there are two children? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there are two (he will also receive the same reward and recompense). The narrator named Mahmood says: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both): I think you people should have also asked, what if there is one? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have said, if there is one (he will also receive this reward and recompense). So Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah! I also think the same."
"2947","The people informed him: His (son) has passed away. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to his father: Do you not like that whichever door of Paradise you come to, you will find him waiting for you?"
"2948","The angels reply: Yes. Allah Almighty says: Did you seize the fruit of his heart (meaning a piece of his liver)? The angels say: Yes. Allah Almighty asks: What did my servant say then? The angels say: He recited 'Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un' and praised You. So Allah Almighty says: Build a house in Paradise for this person and name it 'Bayt al-Hamd' (the House of Praise)."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: The narrator named Abu Talhah Khawani's name is Na'eem bin Ziyad, and he is among the leaders of the people of Syria. From him, Mu'awiyah bin Salih and other people of his city have narrated traditions. The narrator named Abu Sinan is Shaybani. He came to Basra. The people of Basra recorded hadiths from him. His name is Sa'id bin Sinan, while the narrator named Abu Sinan Kufi's name is Dhirar bin Murrah.)"
"2949","I seek the reward of my calamity in Your presence, so grant me its reward and grant me a better substitute in place of what has been lost.” Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When Sayyiduna Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, I recited this supplication and I said: O Allah, grant me better than him. Then I thought, who could be better than Sayyiduna Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him)? When Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) completed her waiting period (‘iddah), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent her a marriage proposal, but she did not marry Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent her a marriage proposal, but she did not marry Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) either. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Umar ibn Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) to her with his proposal. She said: Inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that I am a woman with a temper and I am a woman afflicted by calamity (i.e., I have become a widow), and none of my guardians are present here. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him about this. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Go back to her and say: As for your saying that you are a woman with a temper, I will supplicate to Allah Almighty to remove your temper. As for your saying that you are a woman afflicted by calamity (i.e., you have become a widow), your children will suffice for you. And as for your saying that none of your guardians are present here, none of your guardians, whether present or absent, will dislike this. So Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her son: O Umar! Get up and marry me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). So he married her to him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to her house to spend the night. When Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), she took her daughter Zaynab and seated her in her lap. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) then left. This news reached Sayyiduna Ammar ibn Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him), who was her foster brother. He came to Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: Where is the girl because of whom you caused discomfort to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? Then he took the girl and took her with him. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came again, looked around the corners of the house, and asked: What did you do with Zaynab? Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him: Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and took the girl with him. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) spent the night at Sayyida Umm Salamah’s (may Allah be pleased with her) house. He said: I will not reduce anything from what I have given to such-and-such (wife). There are two mills, two bags, and a mattress filled with leaves. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If I stay with you for seven days, I will also stay with the other wives for seven days. Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The wording of the chain is narrated by Ibrahim ibn Hajjaj and the wording of the text is narrated by Yazid ibn Harun."",""When Abu Salamah died"",""I said this supplication and every time I said it"","" I saw that Allah replaced my calamity with something better. I said to myself"","" """"Who is better than Abu Salamah?"""""",""When her waiting period ended"",""Abu Bakr proposed to her"","" but she did not marry him. Then Umar proposed to her"","" but she did not marry him either. Then the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) sent Umar ibn Al-Khattab to propose to her on his behalf. She said"","" """"Inform the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) that I am a woman who is not interested in remarrying"","" and I am a woman who is already afflicted. And there is no witness among my guardians."""" So the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) went to her and mentioned this to her. He said"","" """"Tell her that when you say"","" 'I am a woman who is not interested in remarrying"",""' I ask Allah to remove your unwillingness. And when you say"","" 'I am a woman who is already afflicted"",""' may your children be sufficient for you. And when you say"","" 'There is no witness among my guardians"",""' no one among your guardians will be a witness"","" nor will anyone who is absent like that."""""",""She said to her son"",""""""O Umar"","" go and marry me to the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him)."""" So Umar married her to him. The Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) used to visit her in her room to be intimate with her. But when she saw him"","" she would take her daughter Zainab and put her in her place. The Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) noticed this"","" so Ammar ibn Yasir"","" who was her foster brother"","" came to her and said"","" """"Where is that wickedness with which you have harmed the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him)?"""" He took her and went with her. The Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) came to her and entered her room"","" and he began to strike his forehead against the sides of the house"","" saying"","" """"What did Zainab do?"""" She said"","" """"Ammar came and took her away."""" So the Messenger of Allah (Peace be upon him) rebuilt the house for her and said"","" """"I will not decrease your status from what I have given to other women"","" two Rahas (sheep) and two Dirhams"","" and a bone filled with stuffing as a headrest."""" And he said"","" """"If I have seven wives"","" I will have the same for all of them."""""""
"2950","Whom do you count as"" Raqub"" amongst you? They (his Companions) said: One who has no children (the children are born unto him but they do not survive). Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: He is not a Raqub but Raqub is one who does not find his child as the forerunner (in Paradise). He then said: Whom do you count as a wrestler amongst you? We said: He who wrestles with persons. He said: No, it is not he but one who controls himself when in a fit of rage. (Using translation from Muslim 2608a)"
"2951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this: 'This is a mercy from your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and a means of death for the righteous people before you. So you all should stay together for it and do not scatter, leaving it.'"" When Sayyiduna Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) heard this, he said: ""He has spoken the truth."
"2952","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him): Once, he heard his father asking Sayyiduna Usamah bin Zaid, ma"
